# Preserve immutable upstream artifacts byte-for-byte.
backend/data/**/raw/** -text
backend/data/**/source-docs/** -text

# Mutable lifecycle and governance artifacts are LF.
#
# These are the files the stage lifecycle tooling rewrites on every stage.
# Without this, a PowerShell writer can silently flip them to CRLF and dirty
# `git diff --check`. Deliberately narrow: this is not repository-wide EOL
# normalization, and it does not touch released data or source bytes.
ROOT-MANIFEST.json text eol=lf
docs/stages/active/CURRENT-STAGE.md text eol=lf
docs/stages/templates/ROOT-STAGE-TEMPLATE.md text eol=lf
# Governed migration bytes are cryptographically bound by the audited candidate
# and the released tree, so they must survive any clone unchanged. Without this,
# a checkout under core.autocrlf=true rewrites them to CRLF and the raw byte
# comparison in terminal migration attribution fails.
#
# Measured on the unfixed arm of a disposable core.autocrlf=true clone. The two
# figures are different scopes and neither is a correction of the other:
#   per file  migration 020 alone carried 442 CRLF pairs and hashed a9d00c46
#             against bound blob ab146237
#   total     all 21 migrations together carried 4446 CRLF pairs, and every one
#             of the 21 diverged from the bound tree
# With this rule applied the same clone measures 0 CRLF pairs and 0 divergences.
backend/db/migrations/*.sql -text